# How seldom one arm of a function that runs often is taken is the weakest estimate that the compiler has. A function that does little more than call another, and that only
# such an arm calls, moves to the arm: nothing is copied, and one call goes. What two arms call stays, and so does a larger body.
# FORM: Prepared
# RUN: pass InlineCalls
# LOSS: MaxInlineHeadBytes

